<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dénes Berinkey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dénes Berinkey was a Hungarian lawyer and politician who served as prime minister of the Hungarian Democratic Republic from January to March 1919, under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi">Mihály Károlyi</a>. His government resigned on 21 March 1919, after the Allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vix-note">Vix Note</a> demanded a further Hungarian withdrawal, and power passed to the Communists, who proclaimed the Hungarian Soviet Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/denes-berinkey.jpg" alt="Dénes Berinkey" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jelfy Gyula · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berinkey_D%C3%A9nes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
